/-!
# Conormal sequence of a projective symmetric-algebra presentation

Source: Stacks Project, Smoothing Ring Maps, proof of Lemma 07CE, equation-sequence
and its splitting; the projective case of More on Algebra, Lemma 07EV
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-symmetric-projective-presentation-conormal).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace Algebra

/-- Source: Stacks Project, proof of Lemma 07CE, lines 357–414, with projective `I/I²`
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-symmetric-projective-presentation-conormal).

Here `P = R[x₁,…,xₙ]`, `A = P/I`, `M = I/I²`, `C = Sym_A(M)`, and `K = ker q`.
The equations on `q`, `φ`, and `α` specify the canonical maps, without introducing
new definitions. The two extensions encode `J/J²` and `L/L²`, where
`J = ker φ` and `L = ker α`. Using `φ.toIntAlgHom` only reinterprets the same ring map;
the extension conormal module has its canonical `C`-module structure.
Tensor factors are written `C ⊗[A] M` and `C ⊗[A] K`, via the tensor swap.
The equivalence `lam` identifies the reduced conormal module with `C ⊗[A] K`.
The equation on `p` says that `lam ∘ p` is reduction modulo `I` on representatives.

Proof. (1) If `A = 0`, all conormal modules and tensor terms are zero. Otherwise the
classes of the generators `f_j` make `q` surjective. Projectivity splits `q`, so
`M ⊕ K ≅ A^m`. By lem-weil-pbc-finite-projective-standard-free-cover choose a common
finite principal-open cover on which both summands are free and lift its elements to `P`.
(2) By lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-coefficient-map-kernel, reduction `Q → A[y]` is surjective
with kernel `IQ`. By lem-weil-pbc-cotangent-complex-symmetric-algebra the map `α` is
surjective and its kernel is generated by the linear forms associated to `K`. Hence `φ`
is surjective. Reduction gives `IQ/(IQ ∩ J²) → J/J² → L/L² → 0`, exact at the last two terms.
(3) Apply lem-weil-pbc-symmetric-algebra-base-change and
lem-weil-pbc-symmetric-algebra-free-module-polynomial on the cover. An adapted basis
identifies `α` with the projection `A[u,v] → A[u]`. Its kernel is generated by the
coordinate variables `v`, a regular sequence (def-weil-pbc-regular-sequence).
By lem-weil-pbc-regular-sequence-conormal-free the linear-form map `lam` is an
isomorphism locally. Its kernel and cokernel vanish globally by
lem-weil-pbc-localization-module-exact and the unit-ideal cover.
(4) Apply lem-weil-pbc-conormal-intersection-regular-quotient on that cover to obtain
`IQ ∩ J² = IQJ` locally, and then globally by lem-weil-pbc-localization-module-exact.
The map `C ⊗_A M → IQ/IQJ`, multiplying a lift of `c` by a representative of `M`,
is well defined; expansion coefficientwise gives its inverse. This identifies the left
term and proves injectivity and exactness, with the displayed formula for `i`.
(5) Compose reduction with the inverse of `lam` to obtain `p` with the stated formula.
(6) Tensor the splitting `M ⊕ K ≅ A^m` with `C` (lem-weil-pbc-tensor-right-exact).
The right term is projective as a summand of `C^m`, so `p` has a linear section.
The split exact sequence gives both displayed conormal-module isomorphisms. -/
theorem symmetric_projective_presentation_conormal
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (n m : ℕ)
    (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)) (f : Fin m → I)
    (hf : Ideal.span (Set.range (fun j ↦ (f j).1)) = I)
    [Module.Projective (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent]
    (q : (Fin m → (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I)) →ₗ[(MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I)] I.Cotangent)
    (hq : ∀ j : Fin m, q (Pi.single j 1) = I.toCotangent (f j))
    (φ : MvPolynomial (Fin m) (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) →+* SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n)
      R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent)
    (hφC : ∀ x : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R,
      φ (MvPolynomial.C x) = algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) (SymmetricAlgebra
        (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent) (Ideal.Quotient.mk I x))
    (hφX : ∀ j : Fin m, φ (MvPolynomial.X j) =
      SymmetricAlgebra.ι (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent (q (Pi.single j 1)))
    (α : MvPolynomial (Fin m) (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) →ₐ[(MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I)]
      SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent)
    (hαX : ∀ j : Fin m, α (MvPolynomial.X j) =
      SymmetricAlgebra.ι (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent (q (Pi.single j 1))) :
    ∃ (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hα : Function.Surjective α),
      ∃ (lam : (SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent) ⊗[(MvPolynomial (Fin n)
        R ⧸ I)] LinearMap.ker q ≃ₗ[SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent]
        (Extension.ofSurjective α hα).Cotangent)
        (i : (SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent) ⊗[(MvPolynomial (Fin n) R
          ⧸ I)] I.Cotangent →ₗ[SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent]
          (Extension.ofSurjective φ.toIntAlgHom hφ).Cotangent)
        (p : (Extension.ofSurjective φ.toIntAlgHom hφ).Cotangent →ₗ[SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial
          (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent] (SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent)
          ⊗[(MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I)] LinearMap.ker q),
        (∀ (c : SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent) (k : LinearMap.ker q)
          (y : (Extension.ofSurjective α hα).ker),
          y.1 = ∑ j : Fin m, MvPolynomial.C (k.1 j) * MvPolynomial.X j →
            lam (c ⊗ₜ k) = c • Extension.Cotangent.mk y) ∧
        (∀ (c : SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent) (x : I) (y :
          (Extension.ofSurjective φ.toIntAlgHom hφ).ker),
          y.1 = MvPolynomial.C x.1 →
            i (c ⊗ₜ I.toCotangent x) = c • Extension.Cotangent.mk y) ∧
        (∀ (x : (Extension.ofSurjective φ.toIntAlgHom hφ).ker) (y : (Extension.ofSurjective α
          hα).ker),
          y.1 = MvPolynomial.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) x.1 →
            lam (p (Extension.Cotangent.mk x)) = Extension.Cotangent.mk y) ∧
        Function.Injective i ∧ Function.Exact i p ∧ Function.Surjective p ∧
        (∃ s : (SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent)
          ⊗[(MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I)] LinearMap.ker q
          →ₗ[SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent]
          (Extension.ofSurjective φ.toIntAlgHom hφ).Cotangent,
          p.comp s = LinearMap.id) ∧
        Nonempty ((Extension.ofSurjective φ.toIntAlgHom hφ).Cotangent ≃ₗ[SymmetricAlgebra
          (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent]
          (SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent) ⊗[(MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸
            I)] (I.Cotangent × LinearMap.ker q)) ∧
        Nonempty ((SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent) ⊗[(MvPolynomial (Fin
          n) R ⧸ I)] (I.Cotangent × LinearMap.ker q)
          ≃ₗ[SymmetricAlgebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent] (Fin m → SymmetricAlgebra
            (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R ⧸ I) I.Cotangent)) := by
  sorry

end Algebra
